Richard and Andy,

I tried changing K but it is still not stable at K=4000 for the NB
mixture and the estimates continue to rise above 150 individuals per
site. The Poisson mixture stabilizes around K= 900. Below is a section
of the survey observations and Poisson mixture model results. I am
using coyote vocal response as count data at sites that have a 2 km
buffer. The observed detection is ~27% for this section. Realistically
the coyotes could move between sites between 2 observation periods as
we calculated collared coyote ranges to be approximately 1.5 to 2
times the size of each survey site.

